{"name":"Mordant Blue","hex":"#2a6671","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mordant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having or showing a sharp or critical quality.","Serving to fix a dye to a fiber."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any substance used to facilitate the fixing of a dye to a fibre; usually a metallic compound which reacts with the dye using chelation.","Any corrosive substance used in etching."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mordant"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mordant","blocks":[{"text":"A mordant or dye fixative is a substance used to set dyes on fabrics. It does this by forming a coordination complex with the dye, which then attaches to the fabric. It may be used for dyeing fabrics or for intensifying stains in cell or tissue preparations. Although mordants are still used, especially by small batch dyers, they have been largely displaced in industry by substantive dyes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Mordant_red_19.png/330px-Mordant_red_19.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mordant","wikidata":"Q5857145"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Indienne%2C_Wesserling.JPG/500px-Indienne%2C_Wesserling.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Indienne%2C_Wesserling.JPG/500px-Indienne%2C_Wesserling.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A French Indienne, a printed or painted textile in the manner of Indian productions, which used mordants to fix the dyes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIndienne%2C_Wesserling.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Dye_rot.jpg/500px-Dye_rot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Dye_rot.jpg/1280px-Dye_rot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Dye_rot.jpg/500px-Dye_rot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dye rot from iron mordant","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADye_rot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Congo-red-2D-skeletal.png/500px-Congo-red-2D-skeletal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.